    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 404,
      "versionNonce": 1289877674,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "pxRn_5__3YxTQBdLBPuPL",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1395.7496049627644,
      "y": 1382.5017132770804,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1382.8125,
      "height": 264,
      "seed": 1271392682,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788712172582,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "Load Balancer for SSE Price Updates\n- Least Connections (stateful SSE) + client reconnects to exact same server if disconnected\n\nHow would the system ensure real-time price updates?\n- the price update service is horizontally scaled\n- price service on update it notifie Redis pub sub which manages our SSE connections to send out on mass price updates\n- Symbol Services then only subscribe to the topics their connected users are subscribed to\n\nHow to ensure high order Consistency?\n- create order entry in our database, set status depending on exchange response\n- run a periodic job to mark \"pending\" orders as failed (after checking exchange again for status)",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Load Balancer for SSE Price Updates\n- Least Connections (stateful SSE) + client reconnects to exact same server if disconnected\n\nHow would the system ensure real-time price updates?\n- the price update service is horizontally scaled\n- price service on update it notifie Redis pub sub which manages our SSE connections to send out on mass price updates\n- Symbol Services then only subscribe to the topics their connected users are subscribed to\n\nHow to ensure high order Consistency?\n- create order entry in our database, set status depending on exchange response\n- run a periodic job to mark \"pending\" orders as failed (after checking exchange again for status)",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 259
    },
